--- !u!114 &6331254282185861334
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>Screen Space Reflections (SSR)</b> for every surface except the ground. In the Volume, add <b>Screen Space Reflection</b>: <i>Mode</i> switched on (not <i>Disabled</i>), <i>Minimum Smoothness</i> 0.25 (rougher surfaces reflect nothing), <i>Smoothness Fade Start</i> 0.35, <i>Max Ray Length</i> 60, <i>Max Ray Steps</i> 128, <i>Roughness Scale</i> \u22123 (sharp reflections, stretched into streaks). SSR can only reflect what is on screen: an object outside the frame, or hidden behind another, is missing from the reflection."
--- !u!114 &7918931559533161963
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>A planar reflection</b> for the ground. A second camera, mirrored below the ground, renders the scene upside down into a texture, and the wet-ground shader reads it. This reflects the haze, which SSR cannot capture well on a rough, bumpy surface.\n\u2022 An empty GameObject <i>Planar Reflection</i> with the <b>Planar Reflection</b> script: <i>Source</i> the Main Camera, <i>Plane Height</i> 0, <i>Resolution Scale</i> 0.5. The script creates its own child <i>Reflection Camera</i>.\n\u2022 Its <i>Culling Mask</i> leaves out the <b>Water</b> layer, so the ground does not block the view from below. Its <i>Volume Mask</i> is Water too: it uses only a second Volume, <i>Planar Reflection Volume (fog only)</i>, placed on the Water layer, whose profile has the fog and nothing else (no colour grading, so the grade is not applied twice).\n\u2022 <i>Reflect Sky</i> off: where the mirrored camera sees the sky, it sees black.\n\u2022 In the ground material: <i>Planar Reflection Strength</i> 3.5, <i>Distortion by the normal</i> 0.03, <i>Vertical stretch</i> 0.35 (the long vertical streaks of light on wet asphalt). <i>Smoothness seen by SSR</i> 0, so SSR does not reflect on the ground a second time."
--- !u!114 &8724715885897543362
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'A smooth surface shows what is around it. Here three things are reflected: the station, the lights and the haze. The scene uses two kinds of reflection together.'
